>
	<h2>Who We Are</h2>
<p>
Dyne.org is a digital community and free software foundry. Born in 1999 from the diaspora of the Freaknet brotherhood, we brought together artists, activists, and hackers from diverse backgrounds to form an online community. We are a think-and-do tank: we share tools, practices, and narratives that empower artists, creatives, and citizens in the digital age.
</p>
<h2>What We Do</h2>
<p>
We offer software development, consulting, training, community infrastructure, and research projects. Our creations include Devuan.org, Dynebolic.org, FreeJ, Frei0r, Tomb, and Interfacer. Numerous individuals and organizations have used and redistributed our work. Our software grants everyone the freedom to use, study, share, and enhance its code, upholding essential liberties.
</p>
<h2>How We Work</h2>
<p>
Three principles guide us. 🫀 Diversity: we mix methods, disciplines, knowledge, culture, languages and our Bastard Culture. 🔬 Open-source: code is our literature, where art, science, and technology meet. ♻️ Ecology: we recycle old technology rather than create needs for new ones, respecting the environment and optimizing resources. 

Join us or donate to keep this work alive. </p>
